+# Admin authentication routing regression
+
+From the full admin repository, after installing its existing dependencies:
+
+```sh
+npm run test:regression:admin-auth
+```
+
+Equivalent command: `node --test tests/admin-auth-routing.test.cjs`.
+
+The tests use esbuild already installed by Vite. They execute the actual ProtectedRoute, Login and access-denied page components with in-memory React/router/storage boundaries. There is no network, browser login, real token, backend request, or permission mutation.
+
+The cases cover allowed ADMIN/admin roles, denied or missing roles, malformed role values, orphan tokens, missing user profiles, incomplete authentication, redirect-chain convergence, and sign-out recovery. Backend authorization remains authoritative; the tests do not validate real account permissions or token signatures.
+
+Run these tests from the full exported/current source checkout. A filtered analysis snapshot that excludes Login.jsx is not a complete runtime checkout and cannot execute this entire suite.
